      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by vectors \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we can use the magnitude of the cross product of these vectors. The cross product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) will give us a vector that is perpendicular to both \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and the magnitude of this vector will be the area of the parallelogram.\n\nThe cross product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n3 & 1 & -2 \\\\\n1 & -3 & 4\n\\end{vmatrix}\n= \\mathbf{i} \\left(1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)\\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left(3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1\\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left(3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i} (4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j} (12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k} (-9 - 1)\n= -2\\mathbf{i} - 14\\mathbf{j} - 10\\mathbf{k}\n= \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of this vector is:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} = \\sqrt{300} = 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the parallelogram is \\(10\\sqrt{3}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the vectors\na = np.array([3, 1, -2])\nb = np.array([1, -3, 4])\n\n# Compute the cross product\ncross_product = np.cross(a, b)\n\n# Compute the magnitude of the cross product\narea = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n17.320508075688775\n```\nThe area of the parallelogram is \\(10\\sqrt{3}\\), which is approximately 17.32. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]",
